      "clinical_diagnosis_basis": "Whole-exome sequencing of the index patient identified the TNFAIP3 nonsense mutation c.A271T: p.(Lys91*), confirmed using PCR and capillary electrophoresis; family with autosomal-dominant inheritance pattern",
      "source_reference_in_review": "not reported",
      "variants": [
        {
          "gene_symbol_as_stated": "TNFAIP3",
          "variant_original_string": "ENSG00000118503:ENST00000433680: exon2:c.A271T: p.(Lys91*)",
          "transcript_as_stated": "ENST00000433680",
          "cdna_hgvs_as_stated": "c.A271T",
          "protein_hgvs_as_stated": "p.(Lys91*)",
          "genomic_coordinates_as_stated": null,
          "variant_type_as_stated": "nonsense",
          "zygosity": "heterozygous",
          "inheritance": "inherited maternal",
          "parental_testing_statement": "Mutation screened in other family members; the mother (I-2) is described as an obligate carrier (she died of liver failure at 46 years)",
          "functional_evidence_statement": "3D modelling (PDB 5LRX) yields a severely truncated protein lacking the complete OTU domain; in HEK293/Flp-In 293 T-REx cells only an N-terminal fragment is expressed (detected only with an N-terminal tag); the p.(Lys91*) mutant failed to suppress TNF-alpha-induced NF-kB activation in a luciferase reporter assay; AP-MS and BioID showed complete loss of interactions with e.g. BRCC3, TRAF2, BIRC2, HUWE1, USP9X, TNIP1, TBK1, CYLD and many weakened interactions; PBMCs of patients II-1 and III-1 showed elevated IL-1beta and IL-18 secretion (canonical and alternative NLRP3 inflammasome activation), increased TNF-alpha secretion, and IL-1beta/IL-18 secretion suppressed by caspase-8 inhibitor Z-IETD-FMK but not by necrostatin-1",
          "pathogenicity_as_stated_by_authors": "predicted to be pathogenic according to the ACMG Standards and Guidelines; loss-of-function mutation",
          "acmg_criteria_as_stated": "not reported"
        }
      ],
